BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Municipal Election All Candidates Event/ Mayoral Debate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T210000
DTSTAMP:20260905T091907Z
UID:0263ff7d-0b17-563e-b9c7-143b8f883623
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to experience local democracy in action!\n\nBurlingt
 onGreen is teaming up with our friends at (https://safestreetshalton.ca/) 
 Safe Streets Halton to host an engaging and informative All-Candidates Mee
 t & Greet & Mayoral Candidates Debate on October 8th. The dual-component e
 vent will also be recorded for post event viewing on BurlingtonGreen’s Y
 outube Channel.\n\n6:00 pm-6:55 pm: All-Candidates Meet and Greet – visi
 t ward and Mayoral candidate information tables to meet the many 2026 Burl
 ington election candidates\n\n7:00 pm-8:30 pm: Mayoral Candidates Debate (
 Moderator: Amy Schnurr\, Executive Director\, BurlingtonGreen) – questio
 ns for the candidates will come from audience members (who have registered
  to attend)\, and will cover a variety of topics.\n\n8:30 pm – 9:00 pm: 
 Closing comments & another opportunity to meet election candidates\n\n*Ple
 ase note that venue space is limited and advance registration is REQUIRED 
 (below).\n\nInquiries: election@burlingtongreen.org\n\n			 				 			 		 Mor
 e Election information and resources (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/news
 /municipal-election-2026/) here.\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/eve
 nts/all-candidates-event-mayoral-debate/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/all-candidates-event-mayoral-de
 bate/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Give Thanks by Caring for Nature
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T120000
DTSTAMP:20260905T091905Z
UID:204a4c1f-ed25-5334-8de6-7c6b9a1cf930
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Thanksgiving by spending time outdoors and giving ba
 ck to the environment. BurlingtonGreen invites you to a Thanksgiving Beach
  Clean-Up\, where community members of all ages can come together to help 
 protect Burlington Beach and learn about the importance of keeping our sho
 reline healthy.\n\nJoin us for a meaningful morning of environmental actio
 n as we remove litter and search for microplastics and nurdles— small pl
 astic pieces that can harm wildlife and make their way into our waterways.
  Through this hands-on activity\, participants will learn how these pollut
 ants impact our environment and how we can all help create cleaner\, healt
 hier spaces for nature and our community.\n\nHosted by: BurlingtonGreen\nW
 hen: Saturday\, October 10th\, 2026 from 10:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m.\nWhere:
  Burlington Beach – meet at BG’s Eco-Hub ( (https://maps.app.goo.gl/mK
 dfqLdN9jqbZHvd8) 1094 Lakeshore Road)\n\nJoin with fellow community member
 s to take action for our environment and learn about local nature with a m
 eaningful day of community engagement!\n\nWhy join?\n\n* Give back to the 
 environment during the Thanksgiving season\n* Help protect Burlington Beac
 h and local wildlife\n* Learn about plastic pollution and solutions\n* Spe
 nd meaningful time outdoors with family and community\n* Connect with othe
 rs who care about protecting nature\n\nThis FREE event is open to everyone
 . Activities take place outdoors\, rain or shine. Please share any accessi
 bility needs with BurlingtonGreen in advance so we can support your partic
 ipation.\n\nGive thanks. Take action. Protect our shoreline. We look forwa
 rd to seeing you at the beach!\n\n2026 COMMUNITY CLEAN UP GREEN UP SUPPORT
 ERS\n\nLEAD SUPPORTERS\n\n(https://www.burlington.ca/en/index.asp)\n\n(htt
 ps://otf.ca/)\n\nCOMMUNITY PARTNER\n\n(https://portal.clubrunner.ca/144/)
 \n\nTREE SPONSOR\n\n(https://burlingtoncentre.ca/sustainability/)\n\nLEAF 
 SPONSORS\n\n(https://rsales.ca/)\n\n(https://bunzlcanada.ca/)\n\n(https://
 www.optimistclubofburlington.com/)\n\n(https://www.optimistclubofburlingto
 n.com/) Junior Optimists of Burlington\n\nSEED SPONSOR\n\n(https://djb.com
 /) DJB Chartered Professional Accountants\n\nHelp BurlingtonGreen (a Regis
 tered Canadian Charity)\, continue to provide impactful\, community-based 
 environmental programs.\nDonations of all amounts are greatly appreciated.
 \n\n(https://www.burlingtongreen.org/donate/) DONATE TODAY!\nURL: https://
 www.burlingtongreen.org/events/thanksgiving-clean-up-2026/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/thanksgiving-clean-up-2026/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annual Tree Photo Contest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T000000
DTSTAMP:20260905T091907Z
UID:3dd1b1a6-5c19-5a9a-be1d-26fc88a1ad00
DESCRIPTION:BG’s annual Tree Photo Contest returns!\n\nGet ready to snap
  a photo of one of your favorite trees in Burlington\, send it to us\, and
  you will be entered into the contest.\n\nThe community will vote for thei
 r favourite photo and the image with the most votes will be the winner of 
 a $50 gift card to Connon Nurseries!\n\nStay tuned for further details and
  (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/tree-photo-contest-2025/) enjoy t
 he photos submitted last year.\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/event
 s/tree-photo-contest-2026/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/tree-photo-contest-2026/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Back to School Beach Clean Up-August 29
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T113000
DTSTAMP:20260905T091906Z
UID:474dd88d-fd8d-504f-9cb1-6b2bbaf3c130
DESCRIPTION:SORRY\, THIS EVENT IS NOW FULL\n\nStart the new school year by
  making a positive impact on our local environment! BurlingtonGreen invite
 s you to our Back to School Beach Clean-Up\, where community members of al
 l ages can come together to help protect Burlington Beach while learning a
 bout the importance of keeping our shoreline healthy and litter-free.\nJoi
 n us for a morning of environmental action as we search for and remove mic
 roplastics and nurdles—tiny plastic pieces that can harm wildlife and en
 ter our waterways.\n\nHosted by: BurlingtonGreen\nWhen: Saturday\, August 
 29th\, 2026 from 9:30 a.m. – 11:30 a.m.\nWhere: Burlington Beach – mee
 t at BG’s Eco-Hub ( (https://g.co/kgs/3ANJBcH) 1094 Lakeshore Road)\n\nN
 ote: Please register in advance\, using the form below.\n\nWhether you’r
 e a student\, family\, educator\, or community member\, this is a great op
 portunity to wrap up the summer by giving back to nature\, connecting with
  others\, and helping create a cleaner\, healthier shoreline for everyone.
 \n\nWhy join?\n\nHelp keep Burlington Beach clean and beautiful\nMake a po
 sitive environmental impact before heading back to school\nLearn about pla
 stic pollution and shoreline stewardship\nConnect with fellow community me
 mbers who care about the environment\nEarn volunteer hours\nEnjoy a fun an
 d meaningful outdoor community event\n\nThis FREE event is open to everyon
 e who wants to make a difference. Whether you’re returning to school\, s
 upporting your family\, or simply looking for a rewarding way to spend you
 r Saturday morning\, we’d love to see you there.\n\nActivities take plac
 e outdoors\, rain or shine. If you have accessibility needs\, please let B
 urlingtonGreen know in advance so we can support your participation.\n\nLe
 t’s head back to school by taking action for a cleaner\, healthier Burli
 ngton Beach. We look forward to seeing you there!\n\n			 				 			 		\n\nUn
 published form\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/back-to-school
 -beach-clean-up-august-29/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/back-to-school-beach-clean-up-a
 ugust-29/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
