 rotect Burlington Beach while learning about the importance of keeping our
  shoreline healthy and litter-free.\n\nJoin us for a morning of environmen
 tal action as we search for and remove microplastics and nurdles—tiny pl
 astic pieces that can harm wildlife and enter our waterways.\n\nHosted by:
  BurlingtonGreen\nWhen: Saturday\, August 15th\, 2026 from 9:30 a.m. – 1
 1:30 a.m.\nWhere: Burlington Beach – meet at BG’s Eco-Hub ( (https://g
 .co/kgs/3ANJBcH) 1094 Lakeshore Road)\n\nNote: Please register in advance
 \, using the form below.\n\nWhether you’re a student\, family\, educator
 \, or community member\, this is a great opportunity to wrap up the summer
  by giving back to nature\, connecting with others\, and helping create a 
 cleaner\, healthier shoreline for everyone.\n\nWhy join?\n\n* Help keep Bu
 rlington Beach clean and beautiful\n* Make a positive environmental impact
  before heading back to school\n* Learn about plastic pollution and shorel
 ine stewardship\n* Connect with fellow community members who care about th
 e environment\n* Earn volunteer hours\n* Enjoy a fun and meaningful outdoo
 r community event\n\nThis FREE event is open to everyone who wants to make
  a difference. Whether you’re returning to school\, supporting your fami
 ly\, or simply looking for a rewarding way to spend your Saturday morning
 \, we’d love to see you there.\n\nActivities take place outdoors\, rain 
 or shine. If you have accessibility needs\, please let BurlingtonGreen kno
 w in advance so we can support your participation.\n\nLet’s head back to
  school by taking action for a cleaner\, healthier Burlington Beach. We lo
 ok forward to seeing you there!\n\nUse the form below to sign up to partic
 ipate.\n\n			 				 			 		\n\nUnpublished form\nURL: https://www.burlington
 green.org/events/back-to-school-beach-clean-up/
