BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ask An Arborist Webinar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T210000
DTSTAMP:20260905T091906Z
UID:540e275a-c9f6-5265-b947-5ff3f973fd61
DESCRIPTION:WEDNESDAY\, SEPTEMBER 23rd @ 7 PM ONLINE WEBINAR!\n\nThe alway
 s popular Kyle McLoughlin\, Master Arborist and Supervisor of Forest Plann
 ing and Health at the City of Burlington\, joins us as our local subject m
 atter expert.\n\nKyle will share another fascinating presentation with tim
 e to follow to address tree-related questions.\n\nWe invite you to send us
  your tree-related questions when you register or email them to us before 
 September 23rd.\n\n*Please note: If you have specific questions about Burl
 ington’s tree-bylaw\, city tree planting/removing/trimming\, please visi
 t the (https://www.burlington.ca/en/services-for-you/Forestry-Operations.a
 sp) City of Burlington website.\n\nBONUS! All Burlington resident attendee
 s will be entered into a draw for a chance to win a FREE tree!\n\n(https:/
 /www.burlingtongreen.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/arborist_event_custom.
 jpg)\n\nLearn about more fall eco-opportunities (https://www.burlingtongre
 en.org/news/fall-events-opportunities/) here.\n\nREGISTER BELOW.\n\nClick 
 (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/news/fall-events-opportunities/) here to 
 learn about more of our fall events and opportunities!\n\nCheck out past A
 sk an Arborist webinars (https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL7K4mljSU5
 jRphqs79ihS00END99O_XbN) here.\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/event
 s/ask-an-arborist-2026/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/ask-an-arborist-2026/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Green Up Community Tree Planting Event
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T113000
DTSTAMP:20260905T091906Z
UID:6eb4f6d1-ace3-5a16-b7ee-a43cde3c391c
DESCRIPTION:Let’s Grow Burlington’s Tree Canopy Together!\n\nSATURDAY
 \, SEPTEMBER 26th @ LONGMOOR PARK\nAdvance Registration Required\n\nBurlin
 gtonGreen and City of Burlington Forestry staff are organizing a community
  tree planting to take place from 9:30 am to noon on Saturday\, September 
 26\, 2026\, at Longmoor Park.\n\nTogether we will plant 500 native trees a
 nd shrubs PLUS some lucky participants will each win a beautiful tree to p
 lant at their Burlington homes!\n\nSpace is limited for this popular event
 .\n\nSign up below.\n\n(https://treecanada.ca/)\n\nThis project was made p
 ossible in large part thanks to a Tree Canada (https://treecanada.ca/grant
 s-awards/community-tree-grants/) Community Tree Grant.\n\n2026 COMMUNITY C
 LEAN UP GREEN UP SUPPORTERS\n\nLEAD SUPPORTERS\n\n(https://www.burlington.
 ca/en/index.asp)\n\n(https://otf.ca/)\n\nCOMMUNITY PARTNER\n\n(https://por
 tal.clubrunner.ca/144/)\n\nTREE SPONSOR\n\n(https://burlingtoncentre.ca/su
 stainability/)\n\nLEAF SPONSORS\n\n(https://rsales.ca/)\n\n(https://bunzlc
 anada.ca/)\n\n(https://www.optimistclubofburlington.com/)\n\n(https://www.
 optimistclubofburlington.com/) Junior Optimists of Burlington\n\nSEED SPON
 SOR\n\n(https://djb.com/) DJB Chartered Professional Accountants\n\nHelp B
 urlingtonGreen (a Registered Canadian Charity)\, continue to provide impac
 tful\, community-based environmental programs.\nDonations of all amounts a
 re greatly appreciated.\n\n(https://www.burlingtongreen.org/donate/) DONAT
 E TODAY!\n\n_\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/green-up-commun
 ity-tree-planting-event/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/green-up-community-tree-plantin
 g-event/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Join us at the beach!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261012T000000
DTSTAMP:20260905T091906Z
UID:79abb066-8970-55db-adf2-8f2db26ab1e5
DESCRIPTION:Our team is leading eco-activities and sharing resources at ou
 r (https://maps.google.com/?cid=5383717800969327865&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwc
 y5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAMYASAF&hl=en-CA&source=embed) Eco Hub
  (1094 Lakeshore Rd) at BeachWay Park.\n\nPop by for a variety of eco-awar
 eness\, advocacy\, and action opportunities\, such as nurdle hunts\, butto
 n making\, microplastic beach clean ups\, seed ball making\, our popular E
 co-Trivia game\, and more!\n\nYou can also visit our (https://www.burlingt
 ongreen.org/bgs-pollinator-garden/) pollinator garden to learn about the i
 mportance of pollinators like bees and butterflies\, and how they support 
 healthy ecosystems.\n\nFollow us on (https://www.facebook.com/burlingtongr
 een) Facebook\, (https://www.instagram.com/burlingtongreenenv/) Instagram
 \, (https://www.linkedin.com/company/burlingtongreen-environmental-associa
 tion/) LinkedIn or (https://bsky.app/profile/burlingtongreen.bsky.social) 
 Bluesky for updates on our week and weekend programming\, 10 am – 4 pm (
 weather permitting).\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/join-us-
 at-the-beach-this-summer/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/join-us-at-the-beach-this-summe
 r/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BG Fun for Kids at RBG!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261004T000000
DTSTAMP:20260905T091906Z
UID:b2574fbd-d0e6-52a9-bd65-ff4733f6e08f
DESCRIPTION:Take a nature walk\, make a seedball and join other eco-fun wi
 th BG at Royal Botanical Gardens on October 3rd and 4th\, 9:30 am to 5:00 
 pm.\n\nBurlingtonGreen will have a tent at the annual (https://tellingtale
 s.org/festivals-events/telling-tales-festival/) Telling Tales Children’s
  Literary Festival in Hendrie Park at the RBG.\n\nHere’s our schedule of
  activities:\n\nDaily 9:45 am – 5 pm – Drop by the BG tent to make you
 r own native wildflower seed balls and learn how you can help protect and 
 nurture butterflies and other pollinators. We’ll also have other all-age
 s eco-fun and climate action resources.\n\nDaily at 11:00 am\, 2:00 pm and
  3:30 pm – Join a Nature Discovery Walk with BG. During this 30 minute g
 uided walk\, you’ll discover fascinating facts about nature all around u
 s. Get inspired to be an eco-champion for special friends like amazing Mon
 arch Butterflies\, and afterwards you can stay to make seedballs to grow w
 ildflowers that can attract butterflies and other pollinators to your own 
 backyard or balcony.\n\nFree entry with (https://tellingtales.org/festival
 -registration/) registration here.\nThen Come find the BG tent in Hendrie 
 Park at the RBG!!\n\n(https://tellingtales.org/festivals-events/telling-ta
 les-festival/) Telling Tales is a weekend of authors\, storytelling\, crea
 tivity and fun! 📖📚🌎\n\n			 				 			 		\n\n(https://www.burlington
 green.org/news/fall-events-opportunities/) Learn about more fall eco-oppor
 tunities\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/bg-fun-for-kids-at-r
 bg/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/bg-fun-for-kids-at-rbg/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tree Loving Care & Planting Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T110000
DTSTAMP:20260905T091905Z
UID:b9913a0f-faf5-579f-bcb3-02ed05e9926c
DESCRIPTION:THURSDAY\, SEPTEMBER 24th @ MOHAWK PARK\nLimited Space\, Advan
 ce Registration Required\n\nOpen to local residents\, students\, groups\, 
 business employees\, while space remains\, this popular tree-ific event is
  fun\, rewarding\, and educational too!\n\nHosted by BurlingtonGreen and C
 ity of Burlington Forestry Staff\, this year’s TLC (Tree Loving Care) wo
 rkshop will bring community members together to carry out some hands-on st
 ewardship activities at (https://maps.app.goo.gl/uehnB2CFTZ9y188j6) Mohawk
  Park in Burlington. The limited capacity event will take place rain or sh
 ine on THURSDAY\, September 24th from 9 am to approximately noon.\n\nSpace
  is limited for this opportunity. Advance registration is required – bel
 ow.\n\nTogether we will plant some native trees\, remove invasive plants a
 nd shrubs from the existing forest at the park\, and tackle some some weed
 ing and adding mulch. We will also create and scatter some native seed bal
 ls too!\n\nThis project is supported by the (https://otf.ca/) Ontario Tril
 lium Foundation.\n\n			 				 			 		\n\nREGISTER FOR THIS EVENT BY COMPLETI
 NG AND SUBMITTING THE FOLLOWING FORM:\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.or
 g/events/tree-loving-care-workshop/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/tree-loving-care-workshop/
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
